	'k4878518b' => 'Midday freight often brings unexpected shortages, split pallets, or damaged cartons. When a carton is missing or crushed, the receiving team catches the discrepancy immediately at the door rather than days later in the aisles. The N1 scanner flags the uncounted unit, and the receiver records a quick damage note using the built-in camera while the delivery driver is still present on the dock. This establishes an objective, factual record before the delivery paperwork is signed and the trailer departs.',
